2026-07-08 15:33:45,566 | AGENT | ProjectCoordinator Agent answered: Our company, Faber IA, approaches project coordination through a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure. This model consists of five phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run. Each phase ends with a formal review and a go/no-go decision point to ensure that all requirements are met before proceeding.

Given the client's specific needs, we would pay particular attention to confidentiality, existing production tools, and seasonality of workload during the framing phase. Our dedicated team, including a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, will work closely with the client to understand their requirements and ensure that our flagship product, Atelier, is tailored to meet their needs.

To maintain confidentiality and preserve professional secrecy, we will leverage our partnership with OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider, which offers SecNumCloud-qualified hosting. This ensures that all data is stored securely and in compliance with relevant regulations.

For integration with existing production tools, we will work with Ligeo Conseil, our integration partner, to ensure seamless connectivity between Atelier and the client's business production tools, such as accounting, payroll, and document management systems.

To address seasonality of workload, we will design the solution to be scalable and flexible, allowing for adjustments to be made as needed to accommodate fluctuations in workload. Our team will also provide change-management and training resources to support the client's staff during the implementation and rollout phases.

Throughout the project, we will maintain a joint steering committee, which meets monthly, and an operational committee, which meets fortnightly, to ensure that all stakeholders are informed and aligned with project progress. We will also use a RACI matrix to formalize roles and responsibilities and provide a single accountable project director as the client's point of contact.

To ensure decision traceability, we will document all decisions made during the project and maintain a clear escalation path in case any issues arise. By following this structured approach, we can ensure that all the client's requirements are met while maintaining confidentiality, reliability, and productivity.
